<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rostislav I of Kiev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1110–1167</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rostislav Mstislavich, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-ii-monomakh">Vladimir Monomakh</a>, was prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> from 1127 and later Grand Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>. He made Smolensk independent of Kiev and in 1136 established a separate bishopric there. His descendants, the Rostislavichi, ruled Smolensk as their own principality and were long contenders for Kiev.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rostislav-i-of-kiev.jpg" alt="Rostislav I of Kiev" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rostislav_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
